MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The smart plug feels like a useful next step because it would let me control a lamp through the Echo devices I have recently added.",
    "The single memory card and HDMI cable fit equipment I use, though I would only choose them once I had a specific storage need or confirmed the cable length."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The Fire TV Stick and Wi-Fi extender repeat needs already covered by my Fire TV Stick 4K Max bundle and NETGEAR extender, with no clear reason to replace either.",
    "The older Fire tablets and wired earbuds do not address a current need, while the card-reader bundle duplicates my existing multiport reader and two extra memory cards lack an identified use."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My recent Alexa purchases seem to have been taken as interest in any Amazon device, although a smart plug adds a useful function and another screen does not currently fill a gap.",
    "My history of buying computer accessories seems to have been taken as a reason to offer more of the same equipment, even when I already have the function covered."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "What I already own matters: an accessory that extends my setup can be more useful than another device that performs the same job.",
    "Compatibility alone does not mean I need something now; a memory card needs a purpose, and an HDMI cable needs to fit the connection and distance I actually need."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my interest in connected home electronics and computer accessories, but miss the difference between extending my setup and duplicating it."
}
